[1m[38;5;231mWhich notification architecture should the design be built on?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mC — Hybrid, pure rules + reconciler (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mDeterministic candidate IDs make dedupe structural; pure testable rules, persistent read/dismiss state, [39m
     [38;5;246mself-healing when tasks change.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m A — Derived, pure computation
     [38;5;246mSimplest possible. No notification history at all; dismissal state needs a stable ID scheme anyway.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m B — Materialized log
     [38;5;246mStored notification records with lifecycle. Real history, but stale/dangling entries and hand-written dedupe.[39m
